      "message": "The logic is already hard to follow here with defers that require tricky ordering placed far from the resources they are connected to.  I think either the defers should all get moved next to their resources and the resources ordered correctly, or use a single defer that handles the ordering.  \n\nFor the first option, move `defer criticalPath.WriteToMetrics(met)` above the `stat` initialization and defer, and move `defer met.Dump` next to where `met` is initialized.  `build.UploadMetrics` seems like it might also have the same problem.\n\nFor the second option, use something like:\n```\ndefer func() {\n    stat.Finish()\n    criticalPath.WriteToMetrics(met)\n    met.Dump(soongMetricsFile)\n    if !config.SkipMetricsUpload() {\n        defer build.UploadMetrics(buildCtx, config, c.simpleOutput, buildStarted, bazelProfileFile, bazelMetricsFile, metricsFiles...)\n    }\n}\n```",
